IMPORT prelude

-- Official Secrets Act 1935 (Singapore) -- what the Act asks of an ordinary person or business: photographs and cameras at
-- prohibited places (ss 3(2), (3), (5), 4), wrongful communication and receipt of official information (s 5), the specified
-- organisations of the Schedule, the evidential presumptions (ss 3(6), 7), the duty to give information on demand (s 10),
-- harbouring (s 11), prosecution consent (s 14), liability of directors and partners (s 16(3)) and the maximum penalties (ss 3(5),
-- 4(1), 17).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/OSA1935.txt. The cover says
-- it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the Schedule annotates later changes, the latest being
-- Act 17 of 2026 with effect from 1 July 2026 (item 7 deleted, item 28 Skills and Workforce Development Agency). SECTION NUMBERS
-- FOLLOW THE BODY: the arrangement at the top of the deposit is one step out of line (it lists "1." with no heading and then
-- "2. Short title"), and the body's own cross-references (s 2 to s 18, s 3(6) to ss 6 and 7) agree with the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0057 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has yet
-- asked a sharper question. SCOPED to the provisions such a person meets. Not encoded: the spying offence of s 3(1) beyond its
-- penalty, the definition of "prohibited place" (taken as a given fact), the Minister's orders on seized photographs (s 3(7), (8)),
-- the uniform, forgery and personation offences of s 6 beyond their penalty, obstruction (s 8), the Minister's warrant for
-- overseas messages (s 9) beyond its penalty, attempts (s 12, same punishment as the offence), arrest and search (ss 13, 15),
-- place of trial and closed hearings (s 16(1), (2)), and ss 17A, 18, 19.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Official Secrets Act 1935`

§§ `3(2), (3) -- photographs of or within a prohibited place`

-- s 3(2): "Any person who takes or makes any photograph, drawing, map, measurement, sounding or survey of or within a prohibited
-- place, shall, unless he proves that the thing so taken or made is not prejudicial to the safety or interests of Singapore and is
-- not intended to be directly or indirectly useful to a foreign Power or to an enemy, be guilty of an offence".
-- Proviso: no offence "to take or make, outside a prohibited place, a photograph or drawing in which such place or part thereof is
-- included, unless it is proved that the photograph or drawing is intended to be prejudicial ... This proviso does not apply to any
-- photograph taken from an aircraft."
-- s 3(3): taking or making in accordance with the terms and conditions of a permit from the competent authority "shall not be an
-- offence under subsection (2)".
-- No purpose prejudicial to Singapore is needed under s 3(2): the burden is on the person to prove the photograph harmless.
GIVEN `taken within the place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `taken from an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `taken under the terms of a permit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the taker proves it harmless` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `an intent to prejudice is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the photograph is an offence under section 3(2)` IF
        (NOT `taken under the terms of a permit`)
    AND (   ((`taken within the place` OR `taken from an aircraft`) AND (NOT `the taker proves it harmless`))
         OR ((NOT `taken within the place`) AND (NOT `taken from an aircraft`) AND `an intent to prejudice is proved`))

§§ `4 -- cameras within a prohibited place`

-- s 4(1): "Any person who within a prohibited place has any apparatus for taking or making photographs in his possession without a
-- permit in writing in that behalf signed by the competent authority shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- to a fine not exceeding $200: Provided that it shall not be an offence ... for any person residing within any prohibited place to
-- possess any such apparatus within that place without a permit."
GIVEN `has a camera within a prohibited place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a signed written permit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `resides within that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `possessing the camera is an offence under section 4` IF
    `has a camera within a prohibited place` AND (NOT `holds a signed written permit`) AND (NOT `resides within that place`)

§§ `2(1) and the Schedule -- specified organisations`

-- s 2(1): "office under the Government" includes any office or employment in or under any department of the Government "or any
-- specified organisation"; "specified organisation" means any organisation specified in the Schedule. The Schedule lists 29 items
-- plus 5A, 11A, 22A and 24A, with items 2 and 7 deleted. A selection, with two bodies the Schedule does not name.
DECLARE Organisation IS ONE OF
    `the Housing and Development Board`
    `the Central Provident Fund Board`
    `the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore`
    `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    `GIC and its subsidiary corporations`
    `the Communicable Diseases Agency`
    `the National Council of Social Service`
    `the Public Transport Council`
    `the Skills and Workforce Development Agency`
    `the Urban Redevelopment Authority`
    `a private bank`
    `the Singapore Tourism Board`

GIVEN `the organisation` IS AN Organisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the organisation is a specified organisation` IF
    CONSIDER `the organisation`
    WHEN `a private bank` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Singapore Tourism Board` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `5(1) -- wrongful communication, use, retention or carelessness`

-- s 5(1): an offence if a person having in his possession or control any secret code word, or any photograph, document or
-- information which (a) "relates to or is used in a prohibited place"; (b) "relates to munitions of war"; (c) "has been made or
-- obtained in contravention of this Act"; (d) "has been entrusted in confidence to him by any person holding office under the
-- Government"; or (e) he obtained or had access to "owing to his position" as a holder (or former holder) of office under the
-- Government, or of a contract made on behalf of the Government or any specified organisation, or as an employee of such a holder,
-- does any of: (f) communicates it to any person other than one he is authorised to communicate it to "or to whom it is his duty to
-- communicate it"; (g) uses it for a foreign Power or "in any manner prejudicial to the safety or interests of Singapore"; (h)
-- retains it "when he has no right to retain it", or fails to comply with lawful directions for its return or disposal; (i) "fails
-- to take reasonable care of" it.
DECLARE Source IS ONE OF
    `information about a prohibited place`
    `information about munitions of war`
    `information obtained in contravention of the Act`
    `information entrusted in confidence by a public officer`
    `information obtained as a public officer or former public officer`
    `information obtained under a contract with a specified organisation`
    `information obtained as an employee of a government contractor`
    `information learned in ordinary private life`

DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `communicating it to an unauthorised person`
    `communicating it to a person he has a duty to tell`
    `using it in a manner prejudicial to Singapore`
    `keeping it with no right to keep it`
    `ignoring a lawful direction to return it`
    `failing to take reasonable care of it`
    `keeping it safely as instructed`

GIVEN `the source` IS A Source
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the information is protected by section 5` IF
    CONSIDER `the source`
    WHEN `information learned in ordinary private life` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is caught by section 5` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `communicating it to a person he has a duty to tell` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `keeping it safely as instructed` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the source` IS A Source, `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence under section 5(1)` IF
    `the information is protected by section 5` `the source` AND `the conduct is caught by section 5` `the conduct`

§§ `5(2) -- receiving`

-- s 5(2): a person who receives any such thing "knowing, or having reasonable ground to believe, at the time when he receives it"
-- that it is communicated to him in contravention of this Act is guilty of an offence "unless he proves that the communication to
-- him ... was contrary to his desire".
GIVEN `knew or had reason to believe it was communicated in breach` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves it was contrary to his desire` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `receiving it is an offence under section 5(2)` IF
    `knew or had reason to believe it was communicated in breach` AND (NOT `proves it was contrary to his desire`)

§§ `5(3), (4) -- former officers working for a foreign government`

-- s 5(3): where a person "is or has been in the employment or service of any foreign Power or government in breach of any
-- undertaking which he has made with the Government or any specified organisation, he shall be deemed to be in possession or control
-- of such information" and to have unlawfully communicated it to a foreign Power or used it prejudicially. (4): "undertaking" means
-- an undertaking IN WRITING not to serve or be employed by any foreign Power or government within a specified period after
-- retirement or resignation "unless he has obtained the prior approval".
GIVEN `served a foreign Power or government` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gave a written undertaking not to` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `obtained prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `within the undertaking's period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unlawful communication is deemed under section 5(3)` IF
        `served a foreign Power or government`
    AND `gave a written undertaking not to`
    AND `within the undertaking's period`
    AND (NOT `obtained prior approval`)

§§ `3(6), 7 -- presumptions`

-- s 3(6): if any document or information "relating to or used in any prohibited place" is made, obtained or communicated "by any
-- person other than a person acting under lawful authority, it shall be deemed to have been made ... for a purpose prejudicial to the
-- safety or interests of Singapore unless the contrary is proved".
GIVEN `relates to a prohibited place` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acting under lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prejudicial purpose is deemed under section 3(6)` IF
    `relates to a prohibited place` AND (NOT `acting under lawful authority`) AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)

-- s 7(2)(a): a person "shall, unless he proves the contrary, be deemed to have been in communication with a foreign agent" if he
-- has, within or without Singapore, (i) visited the address of a foreign agent or consorted or associated with one; or (ii) the name
-- or address of, or other information regarding, a foreign agent has been found in his possession, supplied by him or obtained by
-- him. s 7(1): that communication "shall be evidence" of a prejudicial purpose in proceedings under s 3.
GIVEN `visited or associated with a foreign agent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had a foreign agent's name or address` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves he was not in communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `communication with a foreign agent is deemed under section 7` IF
    (`visited or associated with a foreign agent` OR `had a foreign agent's name or address`) AND (NOT `proves he was not in communication`)

§§ `10 -- the duty to give information on demand`

-- s 10: "It shall be the duty of every person to give on demand to any police officer not below the rank of sergeant, or to any
-- officer of the armed forces on duty, or to any member of the armed forces engaged on guard, sentry, patrol or other similar duty,
-- any information in his power relating to an offence or suspected offence under this Act, and, if so required, and upon tender of
-- his reasonable expenses, to attend at such reasonable time and place as may be specified"; failing to give the information or to
-- attend is an offence. s 18: the Minister may confer "the powers of a police officer not below the rank of sergeant" on any person.
-- (That a constable is below the rank of sergeant is an inference from general knowledge; the Act does not say so.)
DECLARE Demander IS ONE OF
    `a police sergeant`
    `a police inspector`
    `a police constable`
    `a person given sergeant's powers by the Minister`
    `an armed forces officer on duty`
    `a soldier on sentry duty`
    `an off-duty soldier`
    `a private security guard`

GIVEN `the demander` IS A Demander
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the demander may require information under section 10` IF
    CONSIDER `the demander`
    WHEN `a police constable` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an off-duty soldier` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private security guard` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the demander` IS A Demander,
      `about an offence or suspected offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the information is in his power` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gave the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `withholding information is an offence under section 10` IF
        `the demander may require information under section 10` `the demander`
    AND `about an offence or suspected offence under the Act`
    AND `the information is in his power`
    AND (NOT `gave the information`)

GIVEN `required to attend` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonable expenses were tendered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the time and place were reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `attended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to attend is an offence under section 10` IF
    `required to attend` AND `reasonable expenses were tendered` AND `the time and place were reasonable` AND (NOT `attended`)

§§ `11 -- harbouring`

-- s 11(1): an offence if any person "knowingly harbours any person whom he knows, or has reasonable grounds for supposing, to be a
-- person who is about to commit or who has committed an offence under this Act", or knowingly permits such persons to meet in his
-- premises, or having done so "wilfully omits or refuses to disclose to a police officer" information in his power about them.
-- (2): "harbour" includes supplying shelter, food, drink, money, clothes, arms, ammunition or means of conveyance.
GIVEN `knowingly harboured or let them meet` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or had reasonable grounds to suppose an offender` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `wilfully withheld information from the police afterwards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `harbouring is an offence under section 11` IF
        `knew or had reasonable grounds to suppose an offender`
    AND (`knowingly harboured or let them meet` OR `wilfully withheld information from the police afterwards`)

§§ `14 -- the Public Prosecutor's consent`

-- s 14(1): a prosecution "shall not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor", but a person charged may
-- be arrested, and remanded in custody or on bail, before consent; "the case shall not be further prosecuted until that consent has
-- been obtained". (2): before consent "the charge shall be explained to him but he shall not be called upon to plead".
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused may be called upon to plead` IF `the Public Prosecutor has consented`

§§ `16(3) -- directors, officers and partners`

-- s 16(3): where the person guilty is "a company or corporation or a member or an employee of a partnership or firm, acting in the
-- course of the business", every director and officer of the company, or every member of the partnership, "shall be guilty of the
-- like offence unless he proves that the act or omission constituting the offence took place without his knowledge or consent".
GIVEN `the company or firm is guilty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a director, officer or partner` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proves it was without his knowledge or consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is guilty of the like offence` IF
    `the company or firm is guilty` AND `is a director, officer or partner` AND (NOT `proves it was without his knowledge or consent`)

§§ `3(5), 4(1), 17 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 17(1): an offence "by reason of section 3" -- "a fine not exceeding $20,000 and ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14
-- years". (2): ss 5, 6, 8, 11 -- before a District Court $2,000 and 2 years; "with the consent of the Public Prosecutor" may be tried
-- before a Magistrate's Court, $1,000 and 6 months. (3): ss 9, 10 -- the same figures, with no mention of consent for the
-- Magistrate's Court. s 3(5): a false declaration to obtain a permit -- "before a District Court to a fine not exceeding $2,000, or
-- before a Magistrate's Court to a fine not exceeding $1,000", no imprisonment named. s 4(1): camera without a permit -- "a fine not
-- exceeding $200". s 12: attempts, incitement and preparatory acts carry "the same punishment" as the offence.
-- s 3(5) is itself in s 3, so read literally s 17(1) would also reach it; this encoding applies s 3(5)'s own figures (an inference
-- that the specific penalty governs). s 3(2) photographs ARE "by reason of section 3", so they take s 17(1). Imprisonment is in months.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `spying under section 3(1)`
    `a photograph under section 3(2)`
    `a false statement for a permit under section 3(5)`
    `a camera without a permit under section 4`
    `wrongful communication under section 5`
    `uniforms, forgery or personation under section 6`
    `obstruction near a prohibited place under section 8`
    `withholding messages under section 9`
    `withholding information under section 10`
    `harbouring under section 11`

DECLARE Court IS ONE OF
    `a District Court`
    `a Magistrate's Court`

GIVEN `the court` IS A Court, `district figure` IS A NUMBER, `magistrate figure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`by court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the court`
    WHEN `a District Court` THEN `district figure`
    WHEN `a Magistrate's Court` THEN `magistrate figure`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the court` IS A Court
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `spying under section 3(1)` THEN 20000
    WHEN `a photograph under section 3(2)` THEN 20000
    WHEN `a camera without a permit under section 4` THEN 200
    OTHERWISE `by court` `the court` 2000 1000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the court` IS A Court
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `spying under section 3(1)` THEN 168
    WHEN `a photograph under section 3(2)` THEN 168
    WHEN `a false statement for a permit under section 3(5)` THEN 0
    WHEN `a camera without a permit under section 4` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE `by court` `the court` 24 6

-- s 17(2): a Magistrate's Court trial of a s 5, 6, 8 or 11 offence needs the Public Prosecutor's consent; s 17(3) and s 3(5) name a
-- Magistrate's Court penalty with no consent; s 4(1) names no court. For s 3(1) and (2) the Act names only the s 17(1) penalty and,
-- by s 17A, a District Court's full jurisdiction; whether a Magistrate's Court could try them under the Criminal Procedure Code 2010
-- is not decided here, so this rule says only whether THIS ACT provides for it.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the Public Prosecutor consents to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act provides for a Magistrate's Court trial` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `spying under section 3(1)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a photograph under section 3(2)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `wrongful communication under section 5` THEN `the Public Prosecutor consents to it`
    WHEN `uniforms, forgery or personation under section 6` THEN `the Public Prosecutor consents to it`
    WHEN `obstruction near a prohibited place under section 8` THEN `the Public Prosecutor consents to it`
    WHEN `harbouring under section 11` THEN `the Public Prosecutor consents to it`
    OTHERWISE TRUE
